Subject: [PATCH] Fix GUI file-type parity and improve automatic sync

The companion editor only listed 14 audio extensions while the console
transcriber accepts MPEG-1/2 streams, MPEG program streams, 3GPP, WAVE64,
AMR and friends, and it had no way to open a single file. Auto-estimate
also spread words uniformly over the file, so pauses swallowed words.

Supported files
- AUDIO_EXTENSIONS now mirrors (and extends) new_txt_from_audio.py, with
  the same 16-byte content sniffing, so extensionless recordings appear
- Open file... (Ctrl+Shift+O) with grouped filetypes covering every
  supported extension; a folder or a single file can be passed on the CLI
- optional Subfolders scan (also used by the transcriber run)
- natural sort, symlink-loop protection, sync column in the list

Automatic sync
- Auto-estimate runs in a worker thread and uses ffmpeg silencedetect to
  place words in speech runs only, weighted by length and punctuation
- Fill from marks (Ctrl+R) keeps Ctrl+click marks as anchors and spreads
  every other word between them; Ctrl+Shift+click pins and fills at once
- optional Auto-align on load for texts without marks
- reaction lead is a persisted spinbox instead of a constant
- double-click a pinned word to seek to it

Behaviour
- per-user settings (last folder, lead, follow, subfolders, auto-align)
- confirm_discard no longer asks twice after discarding
- dense mark handling no longer does a Text.count per mark on save, and
  the karaoke tag is not rebuilt on every poll
- help/README/TODO updated; new offline tests cover extension parity,
  sniffing parity with the console script, silencedetect parsing, the
  estimates and the settings file
