 ### Automatic timings
 
-* **Auto-estimate** spreads marks over the whole file, weighted by word
-  length (a lead-in and tail are left out). It is a usable starting point
-  for sentence-level highlighting but is not real alignment.
+* **Auto-estimate** first asks FFmpeg (`silencedetect`) where speech runs
+  and where the pauses are, then spreads the words over the speech only,
+  weighted by word length and punctuation pauses. Long silences therefore
+  no longer swallow words, which makes this a useful first pass on
+  dictation and recordings with gaps. Without FFmpeg it falls back to
+  spreading words over the whole file. The run happens in a worker thread,
+  so the GUI keeps playing while it works.
+* **Fill from marks** (`Ctrl+R`) keeps every mark you pinned as a fixed
+  anchor and spreads all remaining words between the anchors, using the
+  same weights. Two or three Ctrl+clicks near the start, middle and end are
+  usually enough for a smooth karaoke track; no anchor is ever moved.
+* **Auto-align on load** (off by default) runs that same estimate in the
+  background whenever a text file is opened and has no marks yet, so a
+  freshly transcribed file already follows the audio without a click. It
+  never replaces existing marks and is skipped when the duration is
+  unknown.
 * **Import timings...** reads whisper-style JSON (`segments[].words[]`,
